WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.499
- What's up?

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:04.560
- I mean, with a last name, like Majors.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.353
You got a military family,
this is incredible.

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:07.440
- Oh yeah.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.273
- It's crazy.

00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:09.106
- Yeah, how are you?

00:00:09.106 --> 00:00:10.650
- I'm good. I feel like I should go

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.393
to the gym after hugging you.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.940
Like when we hugged, I was like

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.280
this is like hugging Lester, my drummer.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.770
It's like a-- just a brick wall man.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.960
Yeah. Do you just work out all the time?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.413
Don't say genetics. I'll slap you.

00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:24.277
(audience laughing)

00:00:24.277 --> 00:00:26.460
Don't you do it.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.800
- I work out a lot.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.633
(audience laughing)

00:00:28.633 --> 00:00:29.466
- Thank you.

00:00:29.466 --> 00:00:30.299
- And when I work out--
- You lie.

00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:31.937
- When I work out

00:00:31.937 --> 00:00:34.200
it feels like there's a
musical theme going on,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.210
with the brothers up there.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.340
Thank you all for your
service, first and foremost.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.173
- Yeah.

00:00:39.173 --> 00:00:41.340
(audience clapping)

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.630
- And Kelly.
- Yeah.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.780
- I would have you know,
that when I work out

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.970
- Oh, what's-?
- What is on my playlist.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.980
- I wanna know. I love that, by the way.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.510
- Since I was a boy.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.301
- No, you did not just
pull up that record.

00:00:54.301 --> 00:00:55.800
(Since U Been Gone by
Kelly Clarkson playing)

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.347
- You already now.

00:00:57.347 --> 00:01:00.828
♪ Here's the thing, we
started out friends ♪

00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:04.464
♪ It was cool, but it was all pretend ♪

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.849
♪ Yeah, yeah ♪

00:01:05.849 --> 00:01:06.682
- You work out to this?

00:01:06.682 --> 00:01:07.551
- This is me.

00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:09.701
♪ Since you been gone ♪

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:12.027
(audience cheering)

00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:14.550
♪ You're dedicated, you took the time ♪

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.133
- Just so you know, this is me.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:21.300
♪ Yeah yeah ♪

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.678
- It's a great song. It's a great song.

00:01:22.678 --> 00:01:23.511
It's a great song.

00:01:23.511 --> 00:01:25.441
(audience cheering)

00:01:25.441 --> 00:01:28.020
- Oh man. It's so funny that you say that.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.704
Cause I hadn't done a show in forever

00:01:29.704 --> 00:01:31.650
and I used to jump up and down.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:32.910
I used to run all over the stage.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.350
I was like crazy. And now I'm just like

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.952
Woo. Holding down this mic stand.

00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:37.103
(audience laughing)

00:01:37.103 --> 00:01:39.210
I love that you love that song.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.014
I would've never guessed
that. It's amazing.

00:01:41.014 --> 00:01:41.847
- [Jonathan] Love it.

00:01:41.847 --> 00:01:44.640
- [Kelly] So what branch of the
military was your family in?

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.660
- Oh, wow. We were--

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.979
My father was in the Air Force.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:51.060
(audience cheering)

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.016
My maternal grandfather was in the Army.

00:01:54.016 --> 00:01:54.990
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.753
- And my paternal
grandfather was in the Navy.

00:01:58.753 --> 00:01:59.586
- Wow.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.477
(audience cheering)

00:02:00.477 --> 00:02:01.604
Covered all the bases. That's incredible.

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:05.040
- Yeah. Yeah. And I was hell
bent on joining the Marines.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.810
- Yeah, you can, I hugged you.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.780
- Tried to do it, but I missed that boat.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.490
- Oh my gosh. So wait,
were your grandfathers

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.680
like a big influence on you growing up?

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.793
- A huge influence.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.453
They were two very different men.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.520
The Navy man was very quiet.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.750
He would sit in this chair.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.200
He was about six five and just kind of

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.780
Yeah, Grandson. Yeah,
Grandson. Yeah, Grandson.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.220
And then my army grandfather

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.800
who I spent all my time
with him on a farm.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.633
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:35.633 --> 00:02:37.137
- Was quite gregarious. But yeah.

00:02:37.137 --> 00:02:39.270
- Also just personalities in general,

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.140
people handle things different.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.897
- Oh yeah. They taught
me so much, you know?

00:02:42.897 --> 00:02:44.700
Don't put your hands in your pocket.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.020
- [Kelly] Yeah. Oh God.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.290
- Ever. Yes sir. No, sir.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.760
I had to get up early in the morning

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.650
feed the chickens or work out.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.000
- Yeah.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.910
- Yeah, I mean, just the
bearing of those two men

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.030
really set me, set me, set me straight.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.210
- So we just saw a bit of
Jonathan's new movie Devotion.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.470
That was intense.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.600
Devotion is based on a true story.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.340
Do you do you appreciate doing

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.990
true stories rather than fiction?

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.330
- Making movies is probably

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.880
one of the most exciting
things in the world.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:15.810
- Just for some.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.340
- [Jonathan] For some.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.210
- Sounds like Hell to others.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.320
- Copy that. Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.520
Well, for me. But telling a true story

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.360
gives a certain amount of stakes.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:28.193
- Yeah. Weight to it.

00:03:28.193 --> 00:03:31.400
- Yeah. Yeah. And you, I like high stakes.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.233
- Yeah.

00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:33.910
- So this story, in particular

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.540
did have a great deal of pressure

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.400
primarily because, you know, as I said

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.838
my grandfathers were in the service.

00:03:41.838 --> 00:03:45.264
And my paternal grandfather,
the guy who, you know

00:03:45.264 --> 00:03:49.770
ran the farm, built
the farm, was in Korea.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:53.486
And this story is about the Korean War.

00:03:53.486 --> 00:03:56.013
About the first black naval aviator.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.230
And he fought in the Korean War.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.839
His name was Ensign Jesse Leroy Brown.

00:04:00.839 --> 00:04:01.890
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.873
- Yeah, there he is. Handsome cat.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.790
And you know, as you
all know, unfortunately

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.400
that war is labeled the forgotten war.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.391
And this is only the second
major motion picture made

00:04:16.391 --> 00:04:19.200
that captures that story.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.428
And for me, talking
about pressure and stakes

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:26.451
to bring that story and
to tell a small glimpse

00:04:26.451 --> 00:04:29.700
of that war and those, you know, soldiers

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.540
- And to honor them.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.830
- Yeah. And to honor them

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.840
on such a grand stage was
extremely high pressure

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.510
and a huge honor.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.370
And we did the best we could.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.170
And I think it's pretty great.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.003
- Oh my God, that's so cool too.

00:04:41.003 --> 00:04:42.678
(audience clapping)

00:04:42.678 --> 00:04:43.511
Like just the relation, like

00:04:43.511 --> 00:04:44.580
with your grandfather having been in it.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.251
That's so cool.

00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:47.084
- Big time. Big time. Big time.

00:04:47.084 --> 00:04:49.470
- Yeah. So did you, did
any pilots take you up

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.090
for like a lesson or anything,
or show you anything?

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.770
- Woo! Did they.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.270
- I flew with the Blue Angels once.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.103
- Did you?

00:04:55.103 --> 00:04:55.936
- I did.

00:04:55.936 --> 00:04:58.350
- Funny, funny, funny,
funny, funny, funny segue.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.770
Our director, JD Dillard, his father

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:05.190
was the second black Blue Angel

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.120
in the history of the Blue Angels.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:06.953
- Oh, really?

00:05:06.953 --> 00:05:07.890
- Yeah. And so we--

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:08.723
- That's incredible.

00:05:08.723 --> 00:05:09.600
- Talk about stakes, man.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.510
We were making this
movie with like, so much

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.240
so much pressure and so much support.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.040
You know, we had guys we
could talk to and say,

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.420
Hey, what was this like?

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.550
And they'd say, It's like
this. You know what I mean?

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.700
And I learned in that
plane what it was like.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.533
- Yeah.

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:29.533
- To a minimal degree.
But it was pretty intense.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.750
Oh yeah. That's my man.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.583
- [Kelly] I love that.
- Yeah.

00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:33.080
- No, I'll tell you, it is intense.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.220
I did well, like the first part.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.390
And then all of a sudden he was like

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.890
you're doing so well. You
want me to do a trick?

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.900
I was like, Hell Yeah. I was
like singing the Top Gun theme.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.864
I was like--

00:05:40.864 --> 00:05:41.697
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:41.697 --> 00:05:42.530
- I was just whatever, stupid.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.300
And then I proceeded
to completely black out

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.814
and barf everywhere after the trick.

00:05:46.814 --> 00:05:47.647
(audience laughing)

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:48.480
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.570
- Cause because he broke the
Gs you weren't supposed to.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:52.403
- [Jonathan] Right.

00:05:52.403 --> 00:05:54.960
- But I literally, there's
video of me going, Yeah.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.370
- [Jonathan] Oh God, yeah yeah yeah.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.920
- It's like crazy. And then--

00:05:58.920 --> 00:05:59.970
- Well, the trick I learned--

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:00.803
- [Kelly] It's hard.

00:06:00.803 --> 00:06:02.467
- Is bananas.

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:03.494
- What, what does that mean?

00:06:03.494 --> 00:06:04.327
- [Jonathan] Bananas.

00:06:04.327 --> 00:06:05.160
- You just eat bananas?

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.080
- Because they taste
the same way going down

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:07.950
as they do coming up.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.277
- For the encore?

00:06:09.277 --> 00:06:10.110
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.210
- Yeah, yeah. And I mean, yeah
we were doing barrel turns.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.530
When you all see the film

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.614
and I hope you guys all
go out and check it out.

00:06:15.614 --> 00:06:20.166
The opening sequence is
myself as Jesse Brown

00:06:20.166 --> 00:06:24.270
and the beautiful Glen
Powell as Tom Huttner.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.867
And we're on a run, a NAF hop.

00:06:27.867 --> 00:06:30.870
NAF hop. Yeah? And we're rolling.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.980
And there's a lighthouse.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.430
And we go right by the lighthouse.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.894
Then we're about 10,
20 feet off the ground

00:06:40.894 --> 00:06:43.590
from the water and you're holding on.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.060
And then they go

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:45.893
and push up.

00:06:45.893 --> 00:06:47.580
And he was like, Do you want come down?

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.170
I said, No sir, I do not wanna come down.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.450
And the truth of the
matter is in that moment

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:52.283
yeah I wanted to go down

00:06:52.283 --> 00:06:53.790
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.920
but I was thinking about, truthfully

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.810
I was thinking about our servicemen.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.186
I was thinking about Jesse.

00:06:59.186 --> 00:07:00.019
- Yeah.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:01.200
- And what he would've gone through.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.316
And for me that's the best exercise

00:07:03.316 --> 00:07:05.250
to get close to the character.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.780
And Jesse Brown

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.250
as you guys will see in
the film, never quit.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.083
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:09.083 --> 00:07:11.030
- And a part of me was
like, There's no way.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.870
There's no way I'm going down.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.840
- I love that you feel so inspired.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.870
- You've gotta honor the character.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.160
And he deserves it.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:21.060
And that was a pretty
pretty gangster move.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.340
- Dude. I know that it
is hard to hold it down

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.453
cause mama didn't.

00:07:24.453 --> 00:07:25.286
- You didn't?

00:07:25.286 --> 00:07:27.330
- No mama came back with like a pink bag

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.466
filled with my vomit.

00:07:28.466 --> 00:07:29.299
(audience laughing)

00:07:29.299 --> 00:07:32.190
But I have to talk about how you're a part

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.990
of the Marvel universe.
I love Marvel as well.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.580
And I love the fact this juxtaposition

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.840
you playing such a serious, like cool

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.060
like historically relevant film

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.950
and then also getting
into the Marvel world,

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.626
which I love that world, too.

00:07:42.626 --> 00:07:43.459
(audience clapping)

00:07:43.459 --> 00:07:46.170
So it's just fun to kinda
exercise those different muscles.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.925
And so you're Kang, right?

00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:49.951
- [Jonathan] I am. I am.

00:07:49.951 --> 00:07:50.784
- [Kelly] You're Kang?

00:07:50.784 --> 00:07:51.617
- [Jonathan] I am Kang, yeah.

00:07:51.617 --> 00:07:53.641
- Yes! We are like
Marvel people. We love--

00:07:53.641 --> 00:07:56.070
I know. No, but I love that.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.530
I love, my favorite thing is when,

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.360
and it's rare when someone comes on here

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.530
and you're doing something that

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.030
like I said, it's like
historically relevant.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:04.500
It's really important, that kinda thing.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.000
But then you do something super fun

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.200
and like just action packed.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.203
I think it's awesome to do.

00:08:09.203 --> 00:08:11.880
Do you like, I would
assume you don't wanna play

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.220
the same role over and
over. So it's kind of fun.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.187
To play a villain?

00:08:15.187 --> 00:08:17.610
- Yeah I mean- a villain. I'm sorry.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.290
A super villain.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.218
- He said super.

00:08:20.218 --> 00:08:21.895
(audience clapping)

00:08:21.895 --> 00:08:23.567
- That's amazing.

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:27.030
- It's extremely humbling, you know?

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.620
And a lot of fun.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:32.890
And you know, I remember
sitting on the incubator

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.880
at my granddaddy's farm.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:36.713
- Yeah.

00:08:36.713 --> 00:08:37.546
- Reading all the books.

00:08:37.546 --> 00:08:38.850
And my imagination would go

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.380
and I would, you know,
play in these worlds.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:44.490
And I never imagined or
perhaps I always hoped

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.170
that I would be able to do that, you know?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.265
- Yeah.

00:08:47.265 --> 00:08:48.408
- Step in the worlds like that.

00:08:48.408 --> 00:08:52.410
And again, Kang is
definitely a dream come true.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.432
You know, for an actor.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:54.265
- It's just fun to play a bad guy.

00:08:54.265 --> 00:08:55.432
- Oh, it's the best.

00:08:55.432 --> 00:08:56.265
- Yeah.

00:08:56.265 --> 00:08:57.300
- It's the best. I mean--

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.370
- You get to be a jerk and
people love it and want it.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:01.170
Who, when can you say that?

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.028
- Yeah, true, true, true.

00:09:02.028 --> 00:09:04.760
And the more jerkish you
are, the more they love you.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:06.630
- Oh my God. It's like more, Yeah.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:07.500
- There's layers to it, you know?

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.333
- Yeah.

00:09:08.333 --> 00:09:09.450
- There's layers.
- How you got there.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:10.820
- There's layers.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:11.653
